{"step_index":960,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:20:48Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-02T23:50:48+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-02T23:50:48+05:30\nShowing lines 85-155 of 216\n85: ):\n86:     contents = await file.read()\n87:     mime_type = file.content_type or \"image/jpeg\"\n88:     \n89:     # Strict prompt with Indian GST invoice extraction rules\n90:     prompt = \"\"\"You are an Indian GST Tax Invoice extractor. Your job is to extract exact numbers and text without dropping digits or inventing items.\n91: \n92: CRITICAL RULES:\n93: 1. COMMA & NUMBER HANDLING (DO NOT DROP DIGITS):\n94:    - In Indian currency notation, commas are thousands separators. NEVER drop digits before commas!\n95:    - Example: '2,535.00' is 2535.0 (Two Thousand Five Hundred Thirty-Five), NOT 535.\n96:    - Example: '1,270.00' is 1270.0 (One Thousand Two Hundred Seventy), NOT 270.\n97:    - Always verify extracted figures against the printed 'Amount/Total in Words' (e.g., 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY RUPEES ONLY' means the total is 4490, not 2173).\n98: \n99: 2. ONLY REAL PRODUCTS/SERVICES IN LINE ITEMS:\n100:    - Extract ONLY genuine products or services from the central invoice table (e.g., 'Bosch All-in-One Metal Hand Tool Kit', 'Taparia Universal Tool Kit').\n101:    - Clean the product description: strip table borders, brackets, or leading/trailing symbols like '[', '|', ']', or unit words like 'NOS'/'PCS'.\n102:    - NEVER extract rubber stamps, signatures, authorization seals, or hand scribbles (e.g., symbols like '©', '~', '|', '[', ']').\n103: \n104: 3. GRAND TOTAL EXTRACTION:\n105:    - Look strictly for the final 'Grand Total', 'Total Amount', 'Net Payable', or 'कुल योग' at the bottom of the invoice (e.g., 4,490.00).\n106:    - DO NOT hallucinate the grand total by summing OCR misreads. Extract the actual printed total on the invoice.\n107: \n108: 4. COLUMN INTEGRITY:\n109:    - Quantity is typically an integer (e.g., 1, 2, 5).\n110:    - Rate is the unit price (e.g., 2535.00, 1270.00).\n111:    - Billed Amount must reflect (Quantity * Unit Rate).\n112: \n113: Extract the invoice details into JSON matching this schema:\n114: - vendor_name: (string)\n115: - gstin: (string or null)\n116: - invoice_number: (string or null)\n117: - date: (string or null)\n118: - items: list of {description, quantity, unit_rate, total_amount}\n119: - subtotal: (number or null)\n120: - cgst: (number or null)\n121: - sgst: (number or null)\n122: - igst: (number or null)\n123: - declared_total: (number or null)\n124: \"\"\"\n125: \n126:     genai_client = get_genai_client(x_api_key)\n127:     if not genai_client:\n128:         return JSONResponse(\n129:             status_code=400,\n130:             content={\"error\": \"Gemini API key is required.\"}\n131:         )\n132: \n133:     # Call Gemini (primary: gemini-2.5-flash; fallback to gemini-3.5-flash if 404/unavailable)\n134:     models_to_try = ['gemini-2.5-flash', 'gemini-3.5-flash', 'gemini-3.8-flash']\n135:     last_err = None\n136: \n137:     for model_name in models_to_try:\n138:         try:\n139:             response = genai_client.models.generate_content(\n140:                 model=model_name,\n141:                 contents=[\n142:                     types.Part.from_bytes(data=contents, mime_type=mime_type),\n143:                     prompt\n144:                 ],\n145:                 config=types.GenerateContentConfig(\n146:                     response_mime_type=\"application/json\",\n147:                     response_schema=ExtractedInvoice,\n148:                     temperature=0.0\n149:                 )\n150:             )\n151:             # Backend Post-Processing & Sanitization\n152:             try:\n153:                 parsed = json.loads(response.text)\n154:                 cleaned = sanitize_and_clean_invoice(parsed)\n155:                 return Response(content=json.dumps(cleaned), media_type=\"application/json\")"}
